## RQ3: Bursty and group arrival processes

Check-in clustering has three possible sources: daily and weekly seasonality, self-excitation (one visit triggers others), and group arrivals. Separate them before attributing bursts to social mechanisms. In crime data, Zhuang & Mateu (2019) found only about 3% of clustering came from self-excitation; daily routine explained most of it.

