**Procedure for choosing the window:**

1. Correct for timestamp rounding first (Kim & Whitt 2014).
2. For each venue-night, compute check-in time gaps for mutually following pairs and for non-following pairs.
3. Take the excess of follower gaps over the non-follower baseline. Set the window where that excess decays to near zero, for example its 90–95th percentile.
4. Report venue rankings at 15, 30 and 60 minutes.
5. Present the fitted dispersion kernel of the cluster model as the data-driven version of the window.

